this system needs the use of a deck of a standard tarot's major arcana.

when a player dies, they will draw 3 cards from the deck. players can only have a maximum of 3 cards.
all cards have 3 keywords associated with them, players can use a card to affect the world based on these vague keywords.
some cards also have specific effects, more powerful but strictly defined.
all cards can also be used in a number of ways to be listed below, often less powerful, but way less situational than the unique powers the cards have.
using a card puts it in the discard pile and gives a trope point to the GM. once the deck is empty, the discard pile is shuffled and replaces the deck.
trope points can be used by the GM to affect the world based on horror media tropes. using a trope point gives back a card to the players, the first one that has space in their hand clockwise from the last person who got a card this way or from the GM if it is the first time.
trope points are always equivalent to the number of cards the dead players are missing.

all cards can be used to:

    augment the size category of a dice for a single roll.

    communicate with the living. the amount of information and what is communicated will depend on the medium used for communication.
        ouija board: the player can move the pointer 1d4 + 1 times
        crystal ball: the player has 6 seconds to describe a purely visual scene.

    affect the world using their keywords:
        0       The fool:
                    spontaneity
                    freedom
                    recklessness
        I       The magician:
                    manifestation
                    power
                    manipulation
        II      The high Priestess:
                    perception
                    wisdom
                    secrets
        III     The empress:
                    beauty
                    abundance
                    dependance
        IV      The empereor:
                    structure
                    retribution
                    inflexibility
        V       The hierophant:
                    conformity
                    wisdom
                    paranoia
        VI      The lovers:
                    relationships
                    emotion
                    conflict
        VII     The chariot:
                    control
                    power
                    opposition
        VIII    Strength:
                    confidence
                    power
                    vulnerability
        IX      The hermit:
                    distance
                    wisdom
                    loneliness
        X       Wheel of fortune:
                    chance
                    abundance
                    repetition
        XI      Justice:
                    law
                    retribution
                    unfairness
        XII     The hanged man:
                    perspective
                    freedom
                    indecision
        XIII    Death:
                    ending
                    renewal
                    inflexibility
        XIV     Temperance:
                    balance
                    wisdom
                    excess
        XV      The devil:
